OL,3,GNEWSAWoman's bid to solve mystery WW1
OL,4,Amedal riddle
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe great niece of an RAF serviceman is
OL,7,Fsearching for information on a "very
OL,8,Funusual" medal awarded to him after
OL,9,FWorld War One.
OL,11,FGill Finnegan, from Darley Abbey in
OL,12,FDerby, owns a silver peace medal
OL,13,Fawarded to her great uncle Thomas Wren
OL,14,Fin 1919.
OL,16,FMany peace medals were handed out to
OL,17,Fchildren in that year, but these were
OL,18,Fnormally made of inexpensive metals
OL,19,Fsuch as pewter or lead.
OL,23,APub: 08-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
